From 4fee4e1d52d248bc8ba7ce70c9cc1b6bb78697ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:02:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Mazak post writes S.. M3/M4 and M5, not
 MOTON/MOTOFF

The Mazak post started the spindle with `MOTON S..` and stopped it with
`MOTOFF`: multi-letter words outside RS-274 / ISO 6983 that state no
direction ahead of a G84 right-hand rigid tap. It now writes `S<rpm> M3`
(`S<rpm> M4` for a left-hand-cut mill, PARAM MillSpindle reverse, #988 -
the post declares millSpindleReverse like fanuc.cps) and `M5`, in the
same places in the program. The Mazak goldens change only on those lines.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/mazak_spindle_words.rs. Decision in
docs/decisions/1411-mazak-iso-spindle.md.

Fixes #1411

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
